  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The industry standard right now is search and regurgitate",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "In standard MoE models (like Mixtral), the \"experts are mathematical layers—feed-forward networks specialized in certain token patterns",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "But in **Dynamic Persona MoE**, the experts are *psychological and methodological profiles*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "If you ask a generic AI, \"What is the state of the market",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The core of this implementation is the   class",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "When you start a project, the system doesn't just grab tools randomly. It classifies the domain. Is this *Threat Analysis*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This ensures we aren't using a hammer to turn a screw. If the domain is Threat Analysis,\" the system knows it needs the   and   personas, not just a generic writer",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "By graphing the methodology, we ensure the AI \"remembers\" *how* it is supposed to be thinking",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s not just drifting through context; it is anchored to a specific analytical approach",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is where the magic happens. Most AI systems are sycophants—they want to agree with you",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is my favorite part of the code. The system actively checks if it is agreeing with itself too much",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "If 80% of the findings are identical across diverse personas, it triggers a **Confirmation Bias** warning",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is how you build a system that *thinks*. It recognizes that total agreement is usually a sign of a blind spot, not truth",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The system is only as good as the experts it summons",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Here is the definition for the **Quantitative Research Specialist**. Notice the  . We aren't just giving it a role; we are giving it a psychological profile (Quantitative: 9, Empathy: low)",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Contrast that with the **Qualitative Specialist**, who is tuned for   and",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "I built this because I was tired of the noise. The internet is a firehose of conflicting narratives, data points, and \"slop",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
